role-boundaries.md (v1.0)
Purpose
Defines the exact capabilities and restrictions for each role in Driv en v1.0. This file is authoritative. No other file may override these rules.
Technician
Primary Purpose: Complete PMs and report equipment issues.
Allowed:
•	View assigned equipment
•	View PM Schedule (assigned only)
•	Complete PMs
•	Upload PM photos
•	Report damage
•	Report safety issues
•	View equipment specs (read only)
Not Allowed:
•	Edit equipment
•	Edit PM templates
•	Edit PM schedules
•	View other technicians’ assignments
•	Access admin dashboards
•	Access customer or vendor tables
Operator
Primary Purpose: Operate equipment and report issues.
Allowed:
•	View equipment assigned to them
•	Report damage
•	Report safety issues
•	View PM status (read only)
Not Allowed:
•	Complete PMs
•	Edit equipment
•	Edit PM schedules
•	Access foreman/manager/admin dashboards
Foreman
Primary Purpose: Oversee crew equipment and PM compliance.
Allowed:
•	View all equipment assigned to their crew
•	View PM status for crew equipment
•	View PM Schedule (crew only)
•	View equipment specs (read only)
Not Allowed:
•	Complete PMs
•	Edit equipment
•	Edit PM templates
•	Edit PM schedules
•	Access manager/admin dashboards
Manager
Primary Purpose: Oversee division level equipment and PM compliance.
Allowed:
•	View all equipment in their division
•	View PM status for division equipment
•	View PM Schedule (division only)
•	View equipment specs (read only)
Not Allowed:
•	Complete PMs
•	Edit equipment
•	Edit PM templates
•	Edit PM schedules
•	Access admin dashboards
Admin
Primary Purpose: Full system access.
Allowed:
•	All equipment
•	All PM schedules
•	All PM templates
•	All divisions
•	All dashboards
•	All settings
•	All data tables
•	All onboarding workflows
Not Allowed:
•	Nothing (full access)
Cross Role Rules
•	No role can “see” another role’s dashboard.
•	No role can “edit” equipment except Admin.
•	No role can “edit” PM templates except Admin.
•	No role can “edit” PM schedules except Admin.
•	No role can “complete” PMs except Technician.
•	No role can “report damage/safety” except Technician + Operator.
